              "id": "text-14",
              "kind": "text",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Carbon Steel AISI 1137 is a general purpose alloy, used for parts that require strength and machinability. It demonstrates good stress resistance, is considered re-sulphurized, and has a machining cost factor of 2.7 in comparison to AISI 12L14. Welding is not ideal due to high sulfur content. 1137 can be annealed, quenched, tempered, and heat treated."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "AISI 1137 Specifications:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "ASTM A29 (1137), ASTM A108, ASTM A311 (1137), ASTM A510 (1137), ASTM A576 (1137)"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "SAE J1397 (1137), SAE J403 (1137), SAE J412 (1137), SAE J414"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "AMS 5020, AMS 5024C, AMS 5024D, AMS 5024"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "QQ-S-637 (1137)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "column-13",
